    <system:String x:Key="Toast.SystemNotification">System Notification</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Toast.SystemNotification.Info" xml:space="preserve">MAA is a portable (non-installed) application. Its notification feature uses the Microsoft.Toolkit.Uwp.Notifications library, which by default registers notifications using the application's executable path.
If you have run MAA from multiple locations, Windows will create separate notification icons (e.g., in the taskbar toast) for each path. This is the default behavior of the library and cannot be controlled or cleaned up automatically by MAA.
To clean up, open the Registry Editor and navigate to:
HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Notifications\Settings
Then delete the entries corresponding to the paths.</system:String>
