    <system:String x:Key="Toolbox.MiniGame.Reclamation.RelaunchAnchor.RA1" xml:space="preserve">Reward estimate: ~159 Mission Acceptance Slip + ~2 Points per run, ~2 min per round

Operator requirement: None

Prerequisite: Clear RA-1 in the main story

Open RA-1 on the map and start the task when &quot;Start&quot; appears at the bottom-right to loop automatically

Note: If you have unlocked technologies related to starting with extra items, please dismantle the facilities in the base that cause starting with extra items, such as Food Supply Stations, Drink Supply Stations, Animal Pens, etc.

Task flow: Automatically executes farming, construction, resource delivery, and settlement loop</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Toolbox.MiniGame.Reclamation.RelaunchAnchor.RA15" xml:space="preserve">Reward estimate: ~500 Mission Acceptance Slip + Points per run, ~2 min per round

Operator requirement: Pramanix the Prerita (support unit allowed)

Prerequisite:
1. Clear RA-15 in the main story
2. Unlock Strategy Business Management. (Hint: RA-3 with Reed the Flame Shadow)
3. If you have Pramanix the Prerita, manually open RA-15 and form a squad once. Use 5 Vanguards (no level requirement) + Pramanix the Prerita, pick her last, then save the squad and exit the stage
4. If you use support Pramanix the Prerita, make sure she is on the first page of the Caster support list (consider adding as friend)

Open RA-15 on the map and start the task when &quot;Start &quot; appears at the bottom-right to loop automatically

Note: If you have unlocked technologies related to starting with extra items, please dismantle the facilities in the base that cause starting with extra items, such as Food Supply Stations, Drink Supply Stations, Animal Pens, etc.

Task flow: Automatically use support operator to execute 60-kill mission</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Toolbox.MiniGame.Reclamation.RelaunchAnchor.RA4" xml:space="preserve">Reward estimate: ~421 Mission Acceptance Slip + ~5 Points per run, ~1 min 40 sec per round

Operator requirement: Wis'adel (support unit allowed)

Prerequisite:
1. Advance the main story until RA-4 is cleared.
2. Unlock Strategy Business Management. (Hint:RA-3 with Reed the Flame Shadow)
3. If you have your own Wis'adel, manually enter the stage and form a team once, ensuring any 5 operators with lower DP cost than Wis'adel + Wis'adel, and Wis'adel is in the 6th slot (i.e., the last one selected). Then confirm recruitment, abandon the current construction, and start from "Start Construction".
4. If using a support Wis'adel, ensure that Wis'adel is on the front page of sniper support units (consider using a friend). Manually enter the stage and add any 5 operators with lower DP cost than Wis'adel, select support Wis'adel for the 6th slot, then confirm recruitment, abandon the current construction, and start from "Start Construction" (ensure the first five slots have operators and the 6th slot is empty).

Open RA-4 on the map and start the task when &quot;Start &quot; appears at the bottom-right to loop automatically

Note: If you have unlocked technologies related to starting with extra items, please dismantle the facilities in the base that cause starting with extra items, such as Food Supply Stations, Drink Supply Stations, Animal Pens, etc.

Task flow: Use the Gold from Strategy Business Management to unlock areas, and use Wis'adel to complete the boss elimination mission.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Toolbox.MiniGame.Reclamation.TalesInSave.Tip" xml:space="preserve">With save file: farm points through crafting:
  1. It must be the first day after settlement, and there should be no enemy attacks entering the stationed area for the next three days.
  2. It must start after entering the interface of the large map. (stationed location needs to be visible)
  3. If the quantity that can be manufactured is exactly a multiple of 99, MAA can get confused (stuck). You can use up a little before saving. This might be repaired later.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Toolbox.MiniGame.Reclamation.TalesNoSave.Tip" xml:space="preserve">Farm points through initial setup: (Be careful that existing save files might be deleted)
  1. After reaching the maximum points, it will output ｢Task Completed｣ and automatically stop the task.
  2. Do not use this task when {key=Game.Operator} is in the Reclamation squad.
  3. Manually check and delete save files to prevent MAA from deleting your valuable saves.
  4. The task must be started from the main screen where ｢Start Reclamation｣ appears at the bottom-right.
  5. If an error occurs during the task or the task completes without reaching the maximum points, please submit an issue on GitHub.</system:String>
